  "notes": "Official cause code from block 13 is 'I' (indeterminate), category left as 'provisional' per FORM-366 fields (category not explicitly given as a named category, so copied as provisional and marked cause.provisional=true). Two parallel, independent failure chains (Train C shaft seal / Train B temp control) converge on the same consequence per rule 5. No stated operable backup system was identified in the narrative for the affected ECCS/HVAC trains during the inoperability window, so no BACKED_UP_BY edges were added. Downstream affected systems (HHSI, LHSI, Containment Spray, CRE HVAC) are modeled as System nodes per explicit statement they were rendered inoperable, but not linked via BACKED_UP_BY since they were themselves inoperable, not backups. No previous similar event citation met the stub-LER criteria (narrative states none exist with this exact failure combination), so no SIMILAR_TO edge/stub LER was created."
